This summer, I had the great opportunity to visity Sweden and join the Nexus of Organic Matter Analytical Developments (NOMAD) Summer school coordinated by [Jeffrey Hawke's](https://www.jeffreyhawkes.com) group.

We stayed at the Tjärno Marine Laboratory and had contact with many great researchers from around the world. Many thanks to all the teachers for the amazing opportunity!

We had the chance to learn a lot about fluorescence-exitation matrix analysis, high-resolution mass spectrometry, NMR and isotopic tracing!!! 
 
